epub: fixed-layout chapter is one viewport-sized page (#1293)

A chapter whose <meta name="viewport"> gives width and height is a
fixed-layout page. mupdf still applied the default @page margin, so
content filling the viewport spilled onto blank extra pages and was
offset from the page edges. Lay such a chapter out at exactly the
viewport size with no page margin, and count it as one page.

diff --git a/source/html/epub-doc.c b/source/html/epub-doc.c
index eb2ad111b..91bab53d8 100644
--- a/source/html/epub-doc.c
+++ b/source/html/epub-doc.c
@@ -177,6 +177,9 @@ static fz_html *epub_get_laid_out_html(fz_context *ctx, epub_document *doc, epub
 
 static int count_laid_out_pages(fz_html *html)
 {
+	/* SumatraPDF: a fixed-layout chapter is one page; overflow is clipped (#1293) */
+	if (html->meta_w > 0 && html->meta_h > 0)
+		return 1;
 	if (html->tree.root->s.layout.b > 0)
 		return ceilf(html->tree.root->s.layout.b / html->page_h);
 	return 1;
